<div class="container prose">
  <h2>Our Mission</h2>
  <p>Kindwell exists to make natural, homeopathic well-being knowledge accessible to everyone. We believe that healing is a process — not a product — and that the right information, shared with compassion, can change lives.</p>
  
  <h2>Where We're Rooted</h2>
  <p>Our community is grounded in the Black Hills of South Dakota — a landscape of ancient pine, quiet rivers, and open sky. This is where our coaches trained, where our traditions live, and where the healing power of nature is most visible.</p>
  
  <p>The Black Hills have long been a place of retreat, reflection, and renewal for many cultures. We carry that spirit into everything we do — patience, respect for natural processes, and a deep belief in the body's own wisdom.</p>

  <h2>What We Believe</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The body knows how to heal itself — our role is to remove obstacles and support the process.</li>
    <li>Less is often more. Gentle, targeted intervention beats aggressive intervention.</li>
    <li>Well-being is holistic: mind, body, spirit, and community all matter equally.</li>
    <li>Knowledge should be accessible, not locked behind gates or hidden in jargon.</li>
    <li>Every person's journey is unique. There are no one-size-fits-all answers.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Our Approach</h2>
  <p>We combine classical homeopathic philosophy with modern understanding of stress, nervous system regulation, and natural wellness. Our content is written in plain language, reviewed for accuracy, and organized so you can find what you need when you need it.</p>

  <p>We are not a medical provider. Kindwell offers educational content, community support, and carefully selected natural products. Always consult your healthcare provider for medical concerns.</p>
</div>

